Subject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?=E2=8F=B3=20feat:=20Count=20Chat=20Retention=20?=
 =?UTF-8?q?From=20the=20Last=20Message?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Under retentionMode: "all" a chat's deadline is fixed when it is created, so a
chat in daily use disappears with all its messages when the period ends.

interface.renewRetentionOnActivity moves the deadline to one retention period
from now when a message is sent. The messages, tool calls, shared links and
subagent threads of the chat move with it, and a chat is rewritten at most once
an hour. Temporary, expired and event-bound chats keep their deadline, and files
keep their own. The switch is off by default.
